  "assumptions": [
    "Daily Q1 table includes every employed agent-day: all agents during Week 1 and only Active agents during Week 2; zero-activity days are retained.",
    "Utilisation = Assigned events / (available agents * 40 attempts/day * 7 calendar days). Week 1 includes the two agents who left at its end; Week 2 excludes them.",
    "Q3 agent-side holds are Late Dispatch, Not Attempted and Agent Time Shortage; all other hold reasons are customer-side.",
    "Q4 counts unique orders held at least once and uses orders.final_status to classify the final outcome.",
    "Q5 return ratio = Returned outcome events / Assigned attempt events; tenure is measured on 26 October 2026 and must be strictly greater than 30 days.",
    "Q6 workday = an agent-day with at least one Assigned event. Fixed salary is monthly salary / 26; Variable pay includes daily allowance per working day and per-delivery allowance on Delivered outcomes. Hold and return charges are event-week costs. Cost per delivered order uses Delivered outcome events in the same week.",
    "Q7 forecasts use the full 14-day observed attempts-per-order ratio by hub. The 85% planning target is applied to the 40-attempt standard, giving 34 planned attempts per agent per day.",
    "For Q8/Q9 H03 stress modelling, Week 2 attempts-per-order is used as a conservative recent baseline. The hold programme reaches 50% reduction of agent-side holds linearly over 14 calendar days, starting 27 October.",
    "New Fixed hires at H04 are assumed to work 26 paid days in the first month. During the first 7 days they operate at 60% of 40 standard attempts/day; thereafter they are planned at 85% of standard."
